DESCRIPTION:You can complete this in your lab notebook or on a google doc.
  \n\nOnce you have completed your lab\, you will document the following:\
 n\nProcedural Description: Include a description of the set up you used an
 d explain why you did what you did.\n\nData Table and graph: Include a rel
 evant Data Table. Then pulling out the relevant information\, create an ap
 proprate graph.\n\nAnalysis: Complete any relevant statistical analysis ne
 eded.\n\nAnalysis Questions: Answer the following below:\n\nAnalyze how th
 e depth of water in the different beakers (shallow vs. deep) affected the 
 rate of water loss over the week. Suggest why water loss might be greater 
 in shallow lakes compared to deeper lakes in natural environments.\n\nComp
 are the water loss between the shaded and unshaded beakers\, and explain h
 ow sunlight exposure and environmental conditions\, such as shading\, infl
 uence the rate of evaporation. Apply this understanding to real-world scen
 arios\, such as managing water loss in reservoirs or lakes in hot\, sunny 
 climates.\n\n 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Model of a Lake conclusion [IB Enviro Systems&Societies HL - Morse]
