 hy you did what you did.</p>\n<p style="padding-left: 40px\;">Data Table a
 nd graph: Include a relevant Data Table. Then pulling out the relevant inf
 ormation\, create an approprate graph.</p>\n<p style="padding-left: 40px\;
 ">Analysis: Complete any relevant statistical analysis needed.</p>\n<p sty
 le="padding-left: 40px\;">Analysis Questions: Answer the following below:<
 /p>\n<p style="padding-left: 80px\;">Analyze how the depth of water in the
  different beakers (shallow vs. deep) affected the rate of water loss over
  the week. Suggest why water loss might be greater in shallow lakes compar
 ed to deeper lakes in natural environments.</p>\n<p style="padding-left: 8
 0px\;">Compare the water loss between the shaded and unshaded beakers\, an
 d explain how sunlight exposure and environmental conditions\, such as sha
 ding\, influence the rate of evaporation. Apply this understanding to real
 -world scenarios\, such as managing water loss in reservoirs or lakes in h
 ot\, sunny climates.</p>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>
