DESCRIPTION:------------------------------------------\nIndependent EE Work
  Session (RRS Required)\n------------------------------------------\n\nGoa
 l: While I conference with seniors\, you will make meaningful progress tow
 ard the EE Café by updating your Research & Reflection Space (RRS).\nNon-
 negotiable: All work must be completed inside your RRS tabs. You will subm
 it evidence (link or screenshots) at the end.\n\n \n\nWhat You Will Submi
 t Today\n--------------------------\n\n* Evidence from each RRS tab (link 
 or screenshots)\n\n* Research Plan (Planning & Writing tab)\n\n* Reflectio
 n 1 (Supervisor Feedback & Reflection tab) ~100 words\n\nWork Through Your
  RRS Tabs (In Order)\n-------------------------------------\n\nRRS Tab 1: 
 Brainstorming (10–15 min)\n------------------------------------\n\nAdd a
  new entry titled: “EE Café Direction Check”\n\n* Topic snapshot: In 
 3–4 sentences\, what is your topic and why does it matter?\n\n* Interest
  + purpose: Why are you personally interested in this investigation?\n\n* 
 EE Café audience: What should a visitor learn at your station in 30 secon
 ds?\n\nRRS Tab 2: Refining Research Question (15–20 min)\n--------------
 -----------------------------------\n\nAdd a new entry titled: “RQ + Met
 hod Fit (2027 EE)”\n\n* Write your current Research Question (RQ).\n\n* 
 Identify your subject and method: What does “good research” look like 
 in your EE subject? (textual analysis\, experiment\, case study\, primary 
 sources\, design/build\, etc.)\n\n* Feasibility check: What evidence/data 
 can you realistically access?\n\n* Ethics check (if applicable): Any conse
 nt\, privacy\, risk\, or data concerns?\n\nQuick standard (2027 EE): Your 
 RQ should clearly align to your subject’s approach and show awareness of
  existing academic knowledge (you are entering a conversation\, not just c
 ollecting facts).\n\nRRS Tab 3: Planning & Writing (25–35 min)\n--------
 ---------------------------------\n\nAdd a new entry titled: “Research P
 lan (Sub-Questions → Sources → Structure)”\n\n* Break your RQ into 3
 –6 sub-questions (these often become body sections/chapter headings).\n\
 n* Create a source plan (use the table below).\n\n* Draft tentative sectio
 n/chapter headings that clearly connect to your sub-questions.\n\n* Identi
 fy gaps + next steps (3–5 specific actions you will do next).\n\nSub-Que
 stion\n\nSources Needed\n\nEvidence Type\n\nStatus\n\n(Write one sub-quest
 ion)\n\n(What sources will answer it?)\n\nprimary / secondary / data / tex
 tual / visual\n\nfound / searching / need help\n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n
  \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\nMini-Lesson: Level Up Your Literature Review
  (Use This in Your Planning)\n--------------------------------------------
 ----------------------------\n\nGear\n\nWhat It Looks Like\n\nWhat You Sho
 uld Do Instead\n\nA: Lower gear\n\nParaphrasing\, summarizing\, describing
  (book-report style)\n\nStart comparing sources: What do they agree/disagr
 ee on? Why?\n\nB: Going up\n\nInterpreting + connecting + contrasting lite
 rature\n\nGroup perspectives into categories (schools of thought / approac
 hes / debates).\n\nC: Top gear\n\nSynthesizing\, being critical\, taking a
  position\, building on literature\n\nWrite 2–3 sentences that show your
  position in the academic conversation:\n“Most scholars argue X / Y. Thi
 s essay builds on that by…”\n\nKey expectation (2027 EE): Your literat
 ure review should show that you understand the academic discourse and can 
 take a justified position within it (not just “summarize sources”).\n\
 nRRS Tab 4: Supervisor Feedback & Reflection (15–20 min)\n--------------
 -----------------------------------------\n\nAdd a new entry titled: “Re
 flection 1: Initial Supervisor Meeting”\n\nLength: ~100 words\n\n* Your 
 ideas about the topic\n\n* Your RQ (current version)\n\n* Initial backgrou
 nd reading/research\n\n* Possible approaches/method\n\n* Early thinking: w
 hat you suspect your answer might be (tentative)\n\nReflection quality tar
 get: Move beyond “what I did.” Include at least one analytical sentenc
 e:\n• What changed in your thinking after meeting your supervisor?\n• 
 What problem do you anticipate\, and what is your plan to handle it?\n\nEx
 it Checklist (Before You Submit)\n----------------------------------\n\n* 
 ✅ Brainstorming tab entry completed\n\n* ✅ Refining RQ tab entry compl
 eted\n\n* ✅ Planning & Writing: sub-questions + source plan + headings +
  next steps\n\n* ✅ Supervisor Feedback & Reflection: Reflection 1 (~100 
 words)\n\n* ✅ Submission uploaded: screenshots for both the Research Pla
 n and Reflection
