CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Please submit the following:\n\n*\n\nYour FINAL line of inquiry
  WITH COLOR CODING\n\n*\n\nA one (1) sentence explanation of the literary 
 or linguistic aspect (authorial choice) you plan to discuss.\n\n*\n\nExamp
 le: Wiesel uses short choppy sentences\, run on sentences\, paragraph brea
 ks\, and incomplete sentences.\n\n*\n\nA two (2) sentence explanation of w
 hat you plan on discussing about the rich idea (argument) and precise cont
 ext.\n\n*\n\nExample: Wiesel gives the reader context clues through his sy
 ntactic choices to help lead them to his implied ideas. Even if the reader
  comes up with a different interpretation\, the choices have been put ther
 e by Wiesel to communicate with the reader\, breaking the wall that exists
  between "author" and "reader."\n\nverb question +\n\nauthor +\n\ntext tit
 le +\n\ngenre +\n\nliterary OR linguistic aspect +\n\nrich idea +\n\npreci
 se context\n\nHow does\, To what extent does\, To what effect does\, etc.\
 n\nWho is the author or what is their role in the text?\n\nWhat is the tit
 le of the work or collection being discussed?\n\nWhat genre does the text 
 belong to?\n\nWhat is the tool the author has used that you’re discussin
 g?\n\n[(Check page 3 of the HLE packet to see examples)] (https://docs.goo
 gle.com/document/d/1ssHqYbplOe9rVhuhO_bvNaPhTSrSVPQ8pJC8HzVFXV0/edit?usp=s
 haring)\n\nWhat’s the idea that you’re trying to prove?\n\nWhat contex
 t is your rich idea happening in?\n\n*\n\nExamples:\n\n*\n\nHow does Marga
 ret Atwood use poetic conventions in her poetry collection Dearly in order
  to critique political decisions that have adverse consequences for the av
 erage citizen?\n\n* Poetic conventions: simile\, metaphor\, rhyme scheme\,
  structure\, aposiopesis\, etc.\n\n*\n\nTo what extent does Naughty Dog’
 s video game “The Last of Us: Part II” use narrative perspective in or
 der to challenge the player’s preconceived notions of protagonist and an
 tagonists?\n\n* Narrative perspective: switching the narrator of the story
  between characters\n\n*\n\nHow does Céline Sciamma use the allusion of O
 rpheus and Eurydice in her film “Portrait of a Lady on Fire” in order 
 to criticize the lack of autonomy that women had over their own fates in t
 he 18th century?\n\n* Allusion: reference to an outside text\, typically B
 iblical or mythological in nature\n\n*\n\nHow does Elie Wiesel use syntact
 ic choices in his memoir Night in order to facilitate the reader in their 
 interpretations of his implied ideas?\n\n*\n\nSyntactic choices: sentence 
 structure\, punctuation\, paragraph breaks\, etc.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:FINAL Line of Inquiry [IB LangA English-Literature HL - Foreman - Y
 L - 25/26]
