DESCRIPTION:Exit Task:\n----------\n\nChoose one of the following situation
 s and explain the ethical challenge it presents: \n\nAutonomous weapons (
 slaughterbots scenario)\n\nSelf-driving car trolley problem \n\nThe surge
 on's organ dilemma\n\nIn your response\, 1) explain the ethical conflict i
 n the scenario\, 2) identify who should be responsible for the decision\, 
 and  3) explain how this situation shows a challenge in applying ethical 
 knowledge to technology. \n\nBonus Insight Point: What makes ethical deci
 sion-making more difficult when machines are involved?\n\n[Exit Tasks & In
 sight Points Explained] (https://ucps.instructure.com/courses/355382/pages
 /exit-tasks-and-insight-points-explained)
