 ot] inhumane. But he had always been an ideologist\, who believed in what 
 he called American individualism'. This approach meant that he policies we
 re inadequate for coping with the enormity of the economic crisis.</span><
 /p>\n<p><span>By the winter of 1932 America was in deep economic trouble. 
 In 1932:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span>Twelve million people were out of wor
 k\; that is a quarter of the country's entire work force</span></li>\n<li>
 <span>The number of people out of work every day was going up at teh rate 
 of 12\,000 every day</span></li>\n<li><span>20\,000 companies went bankrup
