DESCRIPTION:Strategy assesses the extent to which students understand how t
 ensions between perspectives can impact the environmental or societal outc
 omes of a strategy that addresses an issue central to the student’s inve
 stigation. It is based on the following marks:\n\n[image.png] (https://ucp
 s.instructure.com/courses/376418/files/44788651/preview)\n\nClarifications
  for Strategy\n\nThe environmental issue or strategy explored can be diffe
 rent to the one explored in the investigation.\nHowever\, the issue must h
 ave a clearly stated and credible connection to the research question.\nTe
 nsions arise from potentially conflicting goals and needs of groups with d
 ifferent points of view.\n\nDeveloping Your Strategy and Perspective\nWhen
  planning your investigation\, make sure you cover these key elements to c
 onnect your strategy with the research question:\n\n* Link to Your Topic\n
 Describe a clear strategy that directly addresses your environmental topic
  or issue and connects with your research question.\n\n* Use Existing Stra
 tegies\nYour strategy should be based on established methods or approaches
 . Focus on understanding and applying an existing strategy rather than cre
 ating a new one from scratch.\n\n* Identify Tensions\nDiscuss any tensions
  that arise from the strategy\, especially when seen from different viewpo
 ints. For example\, consider how the strategy may have different implicati
 ons or challenges for various stakeholders.\n\n* Present Contrasting Persp
 ectives\nInclude at least two different perspectives or worldviews on the 
 tension you’ve identified. Explain the arguments each perspective might 
 make\, including their potential outcomes.\n\n* Share Your Own View\nAfter
  discussing different perspectives\, include your personal take on the str
 ategy and how you view its potential impact.\n\nYour task: make a copy of 
 the document [Pre-Strategy Assignment] (https://drive.google.com/open?id=1
 6w5GDvAjz3aZ9WhpYGhQ5-Rl-0kvNKwud8ILNYkcVHQ&usp=drive_copy) and complete i
 t and submit below. 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:3- Pre- Strategy [IB Enviro Systems&Societies HL - Morse]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ucps.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _376418&month=03&year=2026#assignment_6993901
