 scourse</span></td>\n<td style="width: 26.6666%\;"><span style="font-famil
 y: georgia\, palatino\;">How language shapes communities\, knowledge\, and
  social power</span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<p><
 span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><strong>Group Discussion Qu
 estions:</strong></span></p>\n<ol style="list-style-type: decimal\;">\n<li
 ><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><strong>Is algospeak best
  understood as linguistic creativity\, historical continuity\, or a strugg
 le over power?</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia
 \, palatino\;"><strong>Does algorithmic moderation change only the <em>for
 m</em> of language\, or can it also change the <em>meaning</em> and circul
 ation of knowledge?</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: ge
 orgia\, palatino\;"><strong>Which linguistic concept from today best expla
 ins algospeak?</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia
 \, palatino\;"><strong>What is gained and what is lost when language adapt
 s itself to technological systems?</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h3>
 <span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\; color: #ba372a\;"><strong>C
 LASS ACTIVITY 4: WHO CONTROLS LANGUAGE ONLINE?</strong></span></h3>\n<p><s
 pan style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">As a whole class\, return to
  the central question:</span></p>\n<table style="border-collapse: collapse
 \; width: 100%\; background-color: #f8cac6\;" border="1">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n
 <td style="width: 100%\;">\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatin
 o\;"><strong>To what extent do technological systems influence the knowled
 ge that can be communicated through language?</strong></span></p>\n</td>\n
 </tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino
 \;">As you discuss\, refer specifically to:</span></p>\n<ul>\n<li><span st
 yle="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">algorithms and moderation</span></
 li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">euphemism and cod
 ed language</span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\
 ;">semantic shift and context collapse</span></li>\n<li><span style="font-
 family: georgia\, palatino\;">language as creativity vs language as power<
 /span></li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h3><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino
 \; color: #cf4a00\;"><strong>EXIT TASK</strong></span></h3>\n<p><span styl
 e="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><strong>To what extent does algospea
 k show that technology shapes what we can know through language?</strong><
 /span></p>\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><strong>In 
 your response\, you must:</strong></span></p>\n<ol style="list-style-type:
  decimal\;">\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Refer to
  <strong>the TED Talk</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: 
 georgia\, palatino\;">Refer to <strong>at least one challenge or complicat
 ion from the article</strong></span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: g
 eorgia\, palatino\;">Use <strong>at least two linguistic concepts</strong>
  from today’s toolbox</span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia
 \, palatino\;">Explain what this suggests about <strong>knowledge\, commun
 ication\, or power</strong></span></li>\n</ol>\n<table style="border-colla
 pse: collapse\; width: 100%\; background-color: #eccafa\;" border="1">\n<t
 body>\n<tr>\n<td style="width: 100%\;">\n<p><span style="font-family: geor
 gia\, palatino\;"><strong>Links to the Exhibition</strong></span></p>\n<p>
 <span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><strong>Prompt 26: Does ou
 r knowledge depend on our interactions with other knowers?</strong></span>
 </p>\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Use today’s les
 son to think about whether our interactions are now mediated by algorithmi
 c systems that shape the language available to us. If that is true\, then 
 to what extent are algorithms influencing how knowers communicate and what
  knowledge circulates between them?</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-famil
 y: georgia\, palatino\;">Possible object ideas: a screenshot of platform m
 oderation guidelines\, a social media post using coded language\, a commen
 t thread where meaning depends on shared context\, or a glossary of online
  terms that changed meaning across communities.</span></p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n
 </tbody>\n</table>\n<p>&nbsp\;</p>\n<div id="assign-to-mount-point"></div>
 \n<div id="choose-editor-mount-point"></div>
END:VEVENT
