DESCRIPTION:FDR & the New Deal\n------------------\n\n[image.png] (https://
 ucps.instructure.com/courses/368381/files/41326673/preview)\n\nHistorical 
 Context:\n\nAims of the New Deal\n\nWhere Hoover had promoted lower taxes\
 , resisted national welfare and had placed the responsibility for aid on s
 tate governments and the voluntary sector\, Roosevelt’s slogans promoted
  the three ‘R’s – Relief\, Recovery and Reform.  He had suggested t
 hat the US needed new legislation to redress the crisis\, a New Deal\, but
  he had offered very little in terms of specific policies for his plan.  
 In fact\, the platform on which his party had stood was a call to reduce f
 ederal spending by 25%\, balance the federal budget\, remove government fr
 om private enterprise and end the ‘extravagant’ farm programs of Hoove
 r.\n\nIn his inaugural address FDR the president stated that the US has 
 ‘nothing to fear but fear itself.’ There was fear in the US that the e
 conomy might not recover\, and genuine hope that the optimism of the new p
 resident would made a difference.  In his address FDR blamed ‘unscrupul
 ous money changes’ for the depression\, but did not suggest that the fed
 eral government's failures and limitations were responsible.\n\nThe First 
 Hundred Days\n\nIn his first Hundred Days\, Roosevelt used all his powers 
 under 'The Trading with the Enemy Act' (which had been passed during the F
 irst World War to give the President extraordinary power without asking fo
 r congressional ratification) to pass fifteen bills and set the future dir
 ection of the first part of the New Deal. The first job was to deal with t
 he banking crisis\; Roosevelt then went on to establish the Alphabet Agenc
 ies. He said he wanted to deliver 'the 3 R's:\n\n* Relief for those suffe
 ring the effects of the Depression\n\n* Recovery of the country to creati
 ng more jobs\n\n* Reform by passing laws to ensure that the people would 
 protected from such an economic disaster happening again.\n\nDirections:\n
 \n* Make an [Individual Copy of today's assignment] (https://docs.google.c
 om/document/d/1wg11vdgHkXHnRolWBPmyWHlltE91gE4HeiUze-PG02Q/copy).\n\n* We'
 ll watch the video clips together in class but they are linked in the assi
 gnment if you need to go back and view them again later. \n\n* Resources 
 you'll need will be your textbook and any internet sources you choose.\n\n
 * Upload your assignment to Canvas when complete. 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:FDR & the New Deal [IB History of the Americas HL - Tesar - YL - 25
 /26]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ucps.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _368381&month=03&year=2026#assignment_6479919
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h3 style="text-align: center\;"><strong>FDR &
 amp\; the New Deal</strong></h3>\n<p><strong><img style="display: block\; 
 margin-left: auto\; margin-right: auto\;" src="https://ucps.instructure.co
