BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTAMP:20260317T040000Z
UID:event-assignment-6479794
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260319
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:What Caused the Great Depression in Canada?\n------------------
 -------------------------\n\nHistorical Context:\n\nThe Depression that st
 arted in the US spread to many countries\; Canada – with its strong econ
 omic ties to the US suffered particularly badly. Between 1929 and 1939\, t
 he Gross Domestic Product fell 40% and unemployment reached 27% by 1933. T
 here are many similarities between the US and Canada regarding both the ca
 uses and impact of the Depression\; the political response however was qui
 te different.\n\nDirections:\n\n* Make a [personal copy of the assignment 
 document] (https://docs.google.com/document/d/16KWgUmso96h26vwemmy-ATr1HIc
 LhaBaXTBbxl0Zph4/copy).\n\n* Using your textbook (Ch. 5 - starting on pg. 
 144) compare and contrast weaknesses and economic vulnerabilities of the A
 merican and Canadian economies prior to 1929.\n\n* You are welcome to disc
 uss and cross-reference with a colleague\, just make sure that your work i
 s your own.\n\n* Submit on Canvas when complete. 
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Causes of the Depression in Canada  [IB History of the Americas HL 
 - Tesar - YL - 25/26]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ucps.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _368381&month=03&year=2026#assignment_6479794
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<h3 style="text-align: center\;"><strong>What 
 Caused the Great Depression in Canada?</strong></h3>\n<p><strong>Historica
 l Context:</strong></p>\n<p><span>The Depression that started in the US sp
 read to many countries\; Canada – with its strong economic ties to the U
 S suffered particularly badly. Between 1929 and 1939\, the Gross Domestic 
 Product fell 40% and unemployment reached 27% by 1933. There are many simi
 larities between the US and Canada regarding both the causes and impact of
  the Depression\; the political response however was quite different.</spa
 n></p>\n<p><strong>Directions:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Make a <a href="htt
 ps://docs.google.com/document/d/16KWgUmso96h26vwemmy-ATr1HIcLhaBaXTBbxl0Zp
 h4/copy">personal copy of the assignment document</a>.</li>\n<li><span>Usi
 ng your textbook (Ch. 5 - starting on pg. 144) compare and contrast weakne
 sses and economic vulnerabilities of the American and Canadian economies p
 rior to 1929.</span></li>\n<li><span>You are welcome to discuss and cross-
 reference with a colleague\, just make sure that your work is your own.</s
 pan></li>\n<li><span>Submit on Canvas when complete.&nbsp\;</span></li>\n<
 /ul>
END:VEVENT
