UID:event-assignment-7126346
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260324
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Practice Exhibition & Prompt Selection\n\nObjective: You will 
 create a practice TOK exhibition by selecting an IA Prompt and linking it 
 to one object. Your object will be selected from a pre-approved list. You
 'll write a 320-word commentary. \n\n1: Refer to your random object\n\nRe
 search and write down everything that you can find or understand about you
 r object: its origins\, its invention\, its use ...\n\n2. Select a prompt
 \n\n* Read through the list of 35 prompts.\n\n* As you do this\, think abo
 ut how they relate to Big Question 1: What is knowledge\, and why does it
  require scrutiny?  and Big Question 2:How does our knowledge influence t
 he way we construct our values? . BQ1 is primarily about the nature of kno
 wledge and how we acquire it\; BQ2 is primarily about the relationship bet
 ween knowledge and values.\n\n* Think also about how the Knowledge & the 
 Knower\, Knowledge & Technology\, and Knowledge & Language themes could a
 ct as a context for what you discuss. BQ1 looks at the core theme: Knowled
 ge & the Knower and BQ2 looks at other themes (e.g.\, technology or langua
 ge)\n\n* These considerations will help you decide which prompt will work 
 best for you. \n\n* What counts as knowledge?\n\n* Are some types of know
 ledge more useful than others?\n\n* What features of knowledge have an imp
 act on its reliability?\n\n* On what grounds might we doubt a claim?\n\n* 
 What counts as good evidence?\n\n* How does the way that we organize or cl
 assify knowledge affect what we know?\n\n* What are the implications of ha
 ving\, or not having\, knowledge?\n\n* To what extent is certainty attaina
 ble?\n\n* Are some types of knowledge less open to interpretation than oth
 ers?\n\n* What challenges are raised by the dissemination and/or communica
 tion of knowledge?\n\n* Can new knowledge change established values or bel
 iefs?\n\n* Is bias inevitable in the production of knowledge?\n\n* How can
  we know that current knowledge is an improvement upon past knowledge?\n\n
 * Does some knowledge belong only to particular communities of knowers?\n\
 n* What constraints are there on the pursuit of knowledge?\n\n* Should som
 e knowledge not be sought on ethical grounds?\n\n* Why do we seek knowledg
 e?\n\n* Are some things unknowable?\n\n* What counts as a good justificati
 on for a claim?\n\n* What is the relationship between personal experience 
 and knowledge?\n\n* What is the relationship between knowledge and culture
 ?\n\n* What role do experts play in influencing our consumption or acquisi
 tion of knowledge?\n\n* How important are material tools in the production
  or acquisition of knowledge?\n\n* How might the context in which knowledg
 e is presented influence whether it is accepted or rejected?\n\n* How can 
 we distinguish between knowledge\, belief\, and opinion?\n\n* Does our kno
 wledge depend on our interactions with other knowers?\n\n* Does all knowle
 dge impose ethical obligations on those who know it?\n\n* To what extent i
 s objectivity possible in the production or acquisition of knowledge?\n\n*
  Who owns knowledge?\n\n* What role does imagination play in producing kno
 wledge about the world?\n\n* How can we judge when evidence is adequate?\n
 \n* What makes a good explanation?\n\n* How is current knowledge shaped by
  its historical development?\n\n* In what ways do our values affect our ac
 quisition of knowledge?\n\n* In what ways do values affect the production 
 of knowledge? \n\nSTEP 3: Take a picture of your object and add it to a G
 oogle Doc. Share your Google Doc with a partner. \n\nThink about what you
  have researched and assign the object to a TOK concept in the themes: Kno
 wledge & the Knower\, Technology\, or Language\n\nStep 3: Writing Your Com
 mentary\n\nYour commentary should:\n\n* Clearly explain the link between t
 he object and the chosen IA prompt\, with explicit references made to the 
 prompt. \n\n* Offer a strong justification for why you have chosen your o
 bject. \n\n* Provide evidence for each of the points you make in your com
 mentary. \n\n* The key qualities of an exhibition are that it should be l
 ucid\, convincing\, and precise. \n\n* Check the rubric below for the pra
 ctice exhibition:\n\n[EX2 The practice TOK exhibition _ Rubric (24-25) (1)
 -1.pdf] (https://ucps.instructure.com/courses/355382/files/45049351?verifi
 er=Pqg4s73VMBMLMe3Qpk8vSbClzD61pHNA1zKE3DMR&wrap=1)[ Download EX2 The prac
 tice TOK exhibition _ Rubric (24-25) (1)-1.pdf] (https://ucps.instructure.
 com/courses/355382/files/45049351/download?verifier=Pqg4s73VMBMLMe3Qpk8vSb
 ClzD61pHNA1zKE3DMR)\n\n[Minimize File Preview] (#)\n\nStep 4: Submitting Y
 our Practice Exhibition File:\n\nThis single file should contain:\n\n* A t
 itle\, that clearly indicates the chosen IA prompt\n\n* An image of your o
 bject\n\n* Your 320-word commentary\n\n* Relevant citations and references
 \n\n* You do NOT need to include an introduction or conclusion. Your comme
 ntary also does NOT have to answer the question in the prompt directly. It
  is a discussion\, rather than a closed response.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Random Object Exhibition Practice [IB Theory of Knowledge - Barron 
 - YL - 25/26]
