  a claim?</li>\n<li>What is the relationship between personal experience a
 nd knowledge?</li>\n<li>What is the relationship between knowledge and cul
 ture?</li>\n<li>What role do experts play in influencing our consumption o
 r acquisition of knowledge?</li>\n<li>How important are material tools in 
 the production or acquisition of knowledge?</li>\n<li>How might the contex
 t in which knowledge is presented influence whether it is accepted or reje
 cted?</li>\n<li>How can we distinguish between knowledge\, belief\, and op
 inion?</li>\n<li>Does our knowledge depend on our interactions with other 
 knowers?</li>\n<li>Does all knowledge impose ethical obligations on those 
 who know it?</li>\n<li>To what extent is objectivity possible in the produ
 ction or acquisition of knowledge?</li>\n<li>Who owns knowledge?</li>\n<li
 >What role does imagination play in producing knowledge about the world?</
 li>\n<li>How can we judge when evidence is adequate?</li>\n<li>What makes 
 a good explanation?</li>\n<li>How is current knowledge shaped by its histo
 rical development?</li>\n<li>In what ways do our values affect our acquisi
 tion of knowledge?</li>\n<li>In what ways do values affect the production 
 of knowledge?&nbsp\;</li>\n</ol>\n</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><sp
 an style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><strong>STEP 3: Take a pictur
 e of your object and add it to a Google Doc. Share your Google Doc with a 
 partner.&nbsp\;</strong></span></p>\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\
 , palatino\;">Think about what you have researched and assign the object t
 o a TOK concept in the themes: Knowledge &amp\; the Knower\, Technology\, 
 or Language</span></p>\n<p><strong><span style="font-family: georgia\, pal
 atino\;">Step 3: Writing Your Commentary</span></strong></p>\n<p><span sty
 le="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Your commentary should:</span></p>\
 n<ol style="list-style-type: decimal\;">\n<li><span style="font-family: ge
 orgia\, palatino\;">Clearly explain the link between the object and the ch
 osen IA prompt\, with explicit references made to the prompt.&nbsp\;</span
 ></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Offer a strong
  justification for why you have chosen your object.&nbsp\;</span></li>\n<l
 i><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Provide evidence for eac
 h of the points you make in your commentary.&nbsp\;</span></li>\n<li><span
  style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">The key qualities of an exhibit
 ion are that it should be lucid\, convincing\, and precise.&nbsp\;</span><
 /li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Check the rubric
  below for the practice exhibition:</span></li>\n</ol>\n<p><span style="fo
 nt-family: georgia\, palatino\;"><span class="instructure_file_holder link
 _holder instructure_file_link_holder"><a class="auto_open file_preview_lin
 k previewable" title="EX2 The practice TOK exhibition _ Rubric (24-25) (1)
 -1.pdf" href="https://ucps.instructure.com/courses/355382/files/45049351?v
 erifier=Pqg4s73VMBMLMe3Qpk8vSbClzD61pHNA1zKE3DMR&amp\;wrap=1" target="_bla
 nk" data-canvas-previewable="false" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="pr
 eview_1" data-api-endpoint="https://ucps.instructure.com/api/v1/courses/35
 5382/files/45049351" data-api-returntype="File">EX2 The practice TOK exhib
 ition _ Rubric (24-25) (1)-1.pdf</a><a class="file_download_btn" style=" t
 ext-decoration: none\;" role="button" href="https://ucps.instructure.com/c
 ourses/355382/files/45049351/download?verifier=Pqg4s73VMBMLMe3Qpk8vSbClzD6
