DTSTART;VALUE=DATE;VALUE=DATE:20260331
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Controversial Aquatic Harvesting\n\nWith this activity\, you wi
 ll have the opportunity to explore and discuss how the harvesting / huntin
 g / collection of a wide variety of species may be considered controversia
 l for a variety of reasons\n\n1) You need to research one of the following
  topics below\, then evaluate the following questions. If you would like t
 o research another controversial topic (must be aquatic) please let me kno
 w.\n\nWhy is this a "controversial harvesting"?\n\nWhy do the people doing
  the harvesting think it is ok?\n\nWhat do you feel about this issue? Just
 ify your thinking using an EVS perspective.\n\n[Shark Finning] (https://yo
 utu.be/388Y1VVBYd8)\n\n[Seal Hunting] (https://youtu.be/mc2t-QJvCGo)\n\n[T
 urtle Egg Collecting] (https://youtu.be/Y7YmymPVB5M)\n\n[Dolphin Hunting] 
 (https://youtu.be/4KRD8e20fBo)\n\n[Whale Hunting] (https://www.youtube.com
 /watch?v=3SmW7_7Q_VA&disable_polymer=true)\n\n2) With this next activity\,
  you will have to opportunity to evaluate preconceived ideas and opinions 
 about the highly controversial issue of aquatic harvesting.\n\nWhaling is 
 the hunting of whales for meat\, oil\, blubber\, and scientific research. 
 Its earliest forms date to at least circa 3000 BC. Read the following arti
 cle from National Geographic on the [History of Whaling] (https://www.nati
 onalgeographic.org/article/big-fish-history-whaling/)\n\nContemporary whal
 ing is subject to intense debate. Pro-whaling countries\, notably Japan\, 
 Norway\, and Iceland\, wish to lift the ban on certain whale stocks for hu
 nting. Anti-whaling countries and environmental groups oppose lifting the 
 ban\n\nRead the following articles to help you understand some more about 
 the cultural and tradition values related to whaling\n\nhttp://www.ifaw.or
 g/united-states/our-work/whales/which-countries-are-still-whaling\n\n[] (h
 ttp://www.ifaw.org/united-states/our-work/whales/which-countries-are-still
 -whaling)http://www.bbc.co.uk/earth/story/20151203-why-do-some-countries-s
 till-hunt-whales\n\n[] (http://www.bbc.co.uk/earth/story/20151203-why-do-s
 ome-countries-still-hunt-whales)http://www.smithsonianmag.com/history/the-
 true-life-horror-that-inspired-moby-dick-17576/\n\n[] (http://www.smithson
 ianmag.com/history/the-true-life-horror-that-inspired-moby-dick-17576/)[In
  the heart of the sea] (https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=K-H35Mpj4uk&t=2s)\
 n\nAfter reading all the articles about what is your perspective of whalin
 g? Think about this from an ecocentric\, anthropcentric or technocentric v
 iewpoint. You must justify your answer.\n\n3) Read the following paragraph
  from a BBC [“Why Do Some Countries Still Hunt Whales”] (http://www.bb
 c.co.uk/earth/story/20151203-why-do-some-countries-still-hunt-whales)\n\nM
 inke whales are found in all of the world's oceans. The International Unio
 n for Conservation of Nature (IUCN) lists them as "least concern"\, meanin
 g they are not in any imminent danger of extinction. The IUCN estimates th
 at there are over 100\,000 minke whales in the wild\, so it should be poss
 ible to continue hunting them without endangering the species.\n\nDoes thi
 s change your opinion from the previous question? Why or why not?\n\n4) Wa
 tch this short YouTube video from a BBC documentary called [“Human Plane
 t”] (https://youtu.be/Z7itOFBPzoY) This may have an effect on your EVS.\
 n\nWhat do you think now?\n\n5) Lastly\, watch this video from [Whale Wars
 ] (https://youtu.be/1jGTFiEnRPY) - a look at the conservation organization
  Sea Shepherd.\n\nWrite a short paragraph summarizing what you have learnt
  in this section. You will score highly if you can use ESS terminology\, u
 se relevant examples and show a good understanding of the topic.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Controversial Aquatic Harvesting [IB Enviro Systems&Societies HL - 
 Morse]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ucps.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _376418&month=03&year=2026#assignment_7126562
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<div id="pageBorders" class="style-scope qowt-
 page"></div>\n<div id="contentsContainer" class="style-scope qowt-page">\n
 <div id="contents" class="style-scope qowt-page">\n<p id="E130" class="x-s
 cope qowt-word-para-0"><span id="E131">Controversial </span><span id="E132
 ">Aquatic </span><span id="E133">Harvesting</span></p>\n<p id="E135" class
 ="x-scope qowt-word-para-1"><span id="E136">With this activity\, </span><s
