DESCRIPTION:Read the section on the hormonal control of the menstrual cycle
  in the [linked article] (https://www.thesciencehive.co.uk/reproduction-in
 -humans-gcse#:~:text=Hormonal%20control%20of%20the%20menstrual\,one%20egg%
 20matures%20per%20cycle.).\n\nFollicle Stimulating Hormone (FSH) and Lutei
 nizing Hormone (LH) are produced by the pituitary gland.\n\nOestradiol (an
  oestrogen) and progesterone are produced by the ovaries.\n\n1) Outline th
 e role of follicle stimulating hormone (FSH) \, luteinizing hormone (LH)\,
  oestradiol and progesterone in regulating the menstrual cycle.\n\n2) Then
 \, use the [interactive animation] (https://schools-assets.abpi.org.uk/ht
 ml-and-swf/2563.html) to follow changes during the menstrual cycle. Then o
 utline how the following changes occur:\n\n* Changes of hormone concentrat
 ions.\n\n* Changes to the endometrium.\n\n* Development and movement of th
 e egg.
SEQUENCE:0
SUMMARY:Menstrual Cycle Hormones [IB Biology HL YL - Morse]
URL;VALUE=URI:https://ucps.instructure.com/calendar?include_contexts=course
 _376462&month=04&year=2026#assignment_7118906
X-ALT-DESC;FMTTYPE=text/html:<p><span>Read the section on the hormonal cont
 rol of the menstrual cycle in the </span><a href="https://www.thesciencehi
 ve.co.uk/reproduction-in-humans-gcse#:~:text=Hormonal%20control%20of%20the
 %20menstrual\,one%20egg%20matures%20per%20cycle."><span>linked article</sp
 an></a><span>.</span></p>\n<p><span>Follicle Stimulating Hormone (FSH) and
  Luteinizing Hormone (LH) are produced by the pituitary gland.</span></p>\
 n<p><span>Oestradiol (an oestrogen) and progesterone are produced by the o
 varies.</span></p>\n<p><strong>1) Outline </strong>the role of follicle st
 imulating hormone (FSH) \, luteinizing hormone (LH)\, oestradiol and proge
 sterone in regulating the menstrual cycle.</p>\n<p>2) Then\, use the&nbsp\
 ;<a href="https://schools-assets.abpi.org.uk/html-and-swf/2563.html"><span
 >interactive animation</span></a><span> to follow changes during the menst
 rual cycle. Then outline how the following changes occur:</span></p>\n<ul>
 \n<li aria-level="1"><span>Changes of hormone concentrations.</span></li>\
 n<li aria-level="1"><span>Changes to the endometrium.</span></li>\n<li ari
 a-level="1"><span>Development and movement of the egg.</span></li>\n</ul>
