 pan style="color: #e03e2d\;"><strong><span style="font-family: georgia\, p
 alatino\;">INTRODUCTION TO THE EE CAFE</span></strong></span></h4>\n<h4><s
 pan style="color: #236fa1\;"><strong><span style="font-family: georgia\, p
 alatino\;">What is the EE Cafe?&nbsp\;</span></strong></span></h4>\n<p><sp
 an style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">A showcase event for your EE-
 in-progress</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;"
 >Designed for feedback\, reflection\, and public sharing</span></p>\n<p><s
 pan style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Audience: teachers\, student
 s\, parents\, and administrators</span></p>\n<p><span style="color: #236fa
 1\;"><strong><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Expectations:
 </span></strong></span></p>\n<p><span style="font-family: georgia\, palati
 no\;">Visual representation of your research (poster\, diagram\, presentat
 ions\, display board\, video)</span></p>\n<p><span style="font-family: geo
 rgia\, palatino\;">Visual explanation (short\, confident summary of your r
 esearch topic) and the following elements that you can answer questions ab
 out:</span></p>\n<ol style="list-style-type: decimal\;">\n<li><span style=
 "font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">RQ and Methodology</span></li>\n<li><s
 pan style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Context and Literature Revie
 w</span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Researc
 h findings so far</span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, pal
 atino\;">Chapter headings or structure (should contain elements from RQ)</
 span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">Problems e
 ncountered</span></li>\n<li><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;
 ">Bibliography (with accurate formatting)</span></li>\n</ol>\n<h4><a class
 ="inline_disabled external" href="https://resources.finalsite.net/images/v
 1616130909/hzscishisnet/mxrti5oecbh4f7afd34y/IB-Extended-Essay-Subject-Spe
 cific-Guide.pdf" target="_blank"><span><span style="color: #e03e2d\;"><str
 ong><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">UNDERSTANDING METHODOL
 OGIES or APPROACHES BY SUBJECT</span></strong></span></span><span class="e
 xternal_link_icon" style=" display: inline-block\; text-indent: initial\;"
  role="presentation"> <span class="screenreader-only">Links to an external
  site.</span></span></a></h4>\n<table style="border-collapse: collapse\; w
 idth: 100%\; height: 696.795px\;" border="1">\n<tbody>\n<tr style="height:
  125.156px\;">\n<td style="width: 49.918%\; height: 125.156px\;"><strong>L
 iterature &amp\; Language</strong></td>\n<td style="width: 49.918%\; heigh
 t: 125.156px\;">The essay should involve analysis of the text(s) in the li
 ght of the RQ. Students may also include a critical perspective on seconda
 ry source material so that the views of critics are used to support the st
 udents' own arguments.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 173.177px\;">\n<td 
 style="width: 49.918%\; height: 173.177px\;"><strong>Sciences: Biology</st
 rong></td>\n<td style="width: 49.918%\; height: 173.177px\;">Students must
  demonstrate that their chosen methods and materials are appropriate for a
 ddressing the RQ. They should explain their rationale for selecting practi
 cal methods. If they undertake experimental work\, they must include suffi
 cient information on their methodology for their work to be repeated.</td>
 \n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 173.177px\;">\n<td style="width: 49.918%\; hei
 ght: 173.177px\;"><strong>Individuals &amp\; Societies: History</strong></
 td>\n<td style="width: 49.918%\; height: 173.177px\;">Where possible\, an 
 attempt should be made to use both primary and secondary sources. They sho
 uld demonstrate both factual material and the opinions of historians. Thes
 e sources must provide sufficient material to develop and support an argum
 ent and conclusion relevant to the research question.&nbsp\;</td>\n</tr>\n
 <tr style="height: 197.17px\;">\n<td style="width: 49.918%\; height: 197.1
 7px\;"><strong>The Arts: Visual Arts</strong></td>\n<td style="width: 49.9
 18%\; height: 197.17px\;">\n<p>If students choose a popular topic well res
 earched by others\, they must attempt to structure an RQ that may lead to 
 a new point of view\, focus\, or interpretation. Sources are expected to i
 nclude visual images\, some of which (depending on research) may be the st
 udents' photographs.</p>\n</td>\n</tr>\n<tr style="height: 28.1146px\;">\n
 <td style="width: 49.918%\; height: 28.1146px\;"></td>\n<td style="width: 
 49.918%\; height: 28.1146px\;"></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p><stron
 g><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">What kinds of data or ev
 idence are valid in your subject?</span></strong></p>\n<p><strong><span st
 yle="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">How do researchers or experts in y
 our subject frame or answer questions?</span></strong></p>\n<p><strong><sp
 an style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">What limitations might apply 
 to search in your subject?</span></strong></p>\n<h4><span style="color: #2
 36fa1\;"><strong><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">ALIGNING 
 RQ WITH METHODS</span></strong></span></h4>\n<p><span style="font-family: 
 georgia\, palatino\;">Take a look at your research question: </span></p>\n
 <p><strong><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;">What is your su
 bject's methodology\, and does your RQ lend itself to it?&nbsp\;</span></s
 trong></p>\n<p>Examples:</p>\n<p><strong>Literature &amp\; Language</stron
 g></p>\n<p><strong>RQ:</strong> How does the use of unreliable narrators i
 n Gothic fiction reflect cultural anxieties of the 19th century?</p>\n<p>
 → <strong data-start="2859" data-end="2870">Method:</strong> Close textu
 al analysis + application of historical literary theory</p>\n<p><strong>Bi
 ology</strong></p>\n<p><strong>RQ:&nbsp\;</strong>What effect does caffein
 e concentration have on the heart rate of Daphnia magna?</p>\n<p>→ <stro
 ng data-start="3045" data-end="3056">Method:</strong> Controlled lab exper
 iment with measurable variables</p>\n<p><strong>Visual Arts</strong></p>\n
 <p><strong>RQ:&nbsp\;</strong>To what extent does Yayo Kusama's art expres
 s trauma through repetition?&nbsp\;</p>\n<p>→ <strong data-start="3213" 
 data-end="3224">Method:</strong> Visual analysis + psychological/artistic 
 theory application</p>\n<h4><span style="font-family: georgia\, palatino\;
